# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Note: Pages serves pages without the .html extension and 308-redirects
# /foo.html to /foo. So destinations here must be extensionless, otherwise
# a "200" proxy rule collapses into a redirect and the browser's URL loses
# the path our JavaScript needs to read.

# Old pathway URLs, kept working.
/pathways.html      /guides             301
/pathways/*         /careers/:splat     301

# /docs and /supabase are hidden by functions instead - Pages _redirects
# cannot return a 404 status.

# The guide pages are now real HTML files, built by build.mjs on every
# deploy, so Cloudflare serves them directly. No proxy rule - and crucially
# Pages applies redirects even when a matching file exists, so leaving them
# here would shadow the files we just built.

# The alumni page became /members when the network widened to include
# current students over 18. Invitation links already sent point at /alumni,
# and so does anything Google has indexed.
/alumni     /members     301
/alumni.html /members    301
